[{"type":"text","text":"\"state_abbr\",\"state_name\"\n\"AK\",\"Alaska\"\n\"AL\",\"Alabama\"\n\"AR\",\"Arkansas\"\n\"AZ\",\"Arizona\"\n\"CA\",\"California\"\n\"CO\",\"Colorado\"\n\"CT\",\"Connecticut\"\n\"DC\",\"District Of Columbia\"\n\"DE\",\"Delaware\"\n\"FL\",\"Florida\"\n\"GA\",\"Georgia\"\n\"HI\",\"Hawaii\"\n\"IA\",\"Iowa\"\n\"ID\",\"Idaho\"\n\"IL\",\"Illinois\"\n\"IN\",\"Indiana\"\n\"KS\",\"Kansas\"\n\"KY\",\"Kentucky\"\n\"LA\",\"Louisiana\"\n\"MA\",\"Massachusetts\"\n\"MD\",\"Maryland\"\n\"ME\",\"Maine\"\n\"MI\",\"Michigan\"\n\"MN\",\"Minnesota\"\n\"MO\",\"Missouri\"\n\"MS\",\"Mississippi\"\n\"MT\",\"Montana\"\n\"NC\",\"North Carolina\"\n\"ND\",\"North Dakota\"\n\"NE\",\"Nebraska\"\n\"NH\",\"New Hampshire\"\n\"NJ\",\"New Jersey\"\n\"NM\",\"New Mexico\"\n\"NV\",\"Nevada\"\n\"NY\",\"New York\"\n\"OH\",\"Ohio\"\n\"OK\",\"Oklahoma\"\n\"OR\",\"Oregon\"\n\"PA\",\"Pennsylvania\"\n\"PR\",\"Puerto Rico\"\n\"RI\",\"Rhode Island\"\n\"SC\",\"South Carolina\"\n\"SD\",\"South Dakota\"\n\"TN\",\"Tennessee\"\n\"TX\",\"Texas\"\n\"UT\",\"Utah\"\n\"VA\",\"Virginia\"\n\"VI\",\"Virgin Islands\"\n\"VT\",\"Vermont\"\n\"WA\",\"Washington\"\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912582345},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see the data includes:\n- The 50 states (AK through WA)\n- DC (District of Columbia)\n- PR (Puerto Rico) - a territory\n- VI (Virgin Islands) - a territory\n\nSo to exclude territories, I should exclude PR and VI. Let me verify the list continues after row 50 (if there are more).","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01QmQkcRybJY2rmwLktiWRKV","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.select('state_abbr', 'state_name').order_by(source.state_abbr).limit(0)","limit":0}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":230,"cacheRead":19511,"cacheWrite":555,"totalTokens":20308,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.0011500000000000002,"cacheRead":0.0019511,"cacheWrite":0.00069375,"total":0.0038068500000000005},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":85},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912582345,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74xPmX1uKoVcnzPvymA","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01QmQkcRybJY2rmwLktiWRKV","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"state_abbr\",\"state_name\"\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912586357},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me check how many rows there are in the farmers_markets table.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_012tnZ4KB9yYF3tjX13QBXey","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.aggregate(count=source.count())"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":130,"cacheRead":20066,"cacheWrite":258,"totalTokens":20467,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0006500000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0020066000000000003,"cacheWrite":0.0003225,"total":0.0029921},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":20},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912586357,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74xfBDqPRN8VqhyPpDS","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_012tnZ4KB9yYF3tjX13QBXey","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"count\"\n53\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912590316},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There are 53 rows. So it seems like there are 50 states + DC + PR + VI = 53 rows total. To exclude territories, I need to exclude PR and VI. Now let me calculate:\n1. Total farmers markets excluding PR and VI\n2. Use the 2025 population of 341,784,857\n3. Calculate the metric\n\nI should create a build script that computes the metric, joining the two data sources. Actually, wait - I need to think about this. The farmers_markets table is organized by state, but I just need the total for the US (excluding territories). So I could:\n\nOption 1: Create a build script that sums farmers_markets excluding PR and VI, joins with the census data, and calculates the metric.\nOption 2: Use xorq_select to get the total farmers markets and the population, then compose a metric.\n\nGiven the guidance in the xorq-catalog skill, for a cross-dataset metric I should create a build script. Let me do that.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Let me create a build script that computes the farmers markets per 100,000 residents by joining the two sources:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_017a6tJpKAthjNf7kZymc1bf","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_metric.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener(); _o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]; u.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"farmers_markets\", storage_options=so)\n\n# Read census population data\npop = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"census_population\", storage_options=so)\n\n# Exclude territories (PR, VI) and sum farmers markets\nfm_total = (fm\n    .filter((fm.state_abbr != 'PR') & (fm.state_abbr != 'VI'))\n    .aggregate(total_markets=fm.farmers_markets.sum())\n    .mutate(key=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Get US population for 2025\nus_pop = (pop\n    .filter(pop.NAME == 'United States')\n    .select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n    .mutate(key=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Join and calculate metric\nexpr = (\n    fm_total.join(us_pop, fm_total.key == us_pop.key)\n      .mutate(markets_per_100k=fm_total.total_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select(\"total_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":837,"cacheRead":20324,"cacheWrite":174,"totalTokens":21347,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.004185,"cacheRead":0.0020324,"cacheWrite":0.0002175,"total":0.0064469},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":231},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912590316,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74xv3S6dB29T8foSEUP","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_017a6tJpKAthjNf7kZymc1bf","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1328 bytes to .xorq/scripts/build_metric.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912598704},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me build this metric.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01LGZWPwrQKR2YjS2m3aM6qD","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-60-s0bla2kb && xorq build .xorq/scripts/build_metric.py --builds-dir .xorq/builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/metric_bp.txt && cat /tmp/metric_bp.txt"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":137,"cacheRead":20498,"cacheWrite":875,"totalTokens":21523,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0006850000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0020498,"cacheWrite":0.00109375,"total":0.00384155},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":12},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912598705,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74yawFpcj93rmfJMB8J","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01LGZWPwrQKR2YjS2m3aM6qD","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Building expr from .xorq/scripts/build_metric.py\n/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-pa